---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Keyboard Shortcuts"
  description="Complete keyboard shortcut reference for the Ash text editor."
>
  <h1>Keyboard Shortcuts</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Ash provides IDE-level keyboard shortcuts. On macOS use <code>Cmd</code>;
    on Windows/Linux use <code>Ctrl</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Formatting</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Shortcut</th>
        <th>Action</th>
        <th>Details</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + B</code></td>
        <td>Bold</td>
        <td>
          Wraps selection in <code>**...**</code>. Press again to toggle off.
          With no selection, inserts <code>****</code> and places cursor between
          the markers.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + I</code></td>
        <td>Italic</td>
        <td>
          Wraps selection in <code>_..._</code>. Press again to toggle off.
          With no selection, inserts <code>__</code> and places cursor between
          the markers.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Indentation</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Shortcut</th>
        <th>Action</th>
        <th>Details</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Tab</code></td>
        <td>Indent</td>
        <td>
          With no selection: inserts spaces at the cursor (respects
          <code>tabSize</code>). With a multi-line selection: indents all
          selected lines.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Shift + Tab</code></td>
        <td>Unindent</td>
        <td>
          Removes up to <code>tabSize</code> spaces from the start of the
          current line (or all selected lines).
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Smart Enter</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Context</th>
        <th>Behavior</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Inside an unordered list item (<code>- </code>, <code>* </code>, <code>+ </code>)</td>
        <td>Pressing Enter creates a new list item with the same bullet and indentation.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>On an empty unordered list item</td>
        <td>Pressing Enter ends the list and creates a blank line.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Inside an ordered list item (<code>1. </code>)</td>
        <td>Pressing Enter creates the next numbered item.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>On an empty ordered list item</td>
        <td>Pressing Enter ends the list.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Inside a blockquote (<code>&gt; </code>)</td>
        <td>Pressing Enter continues the blockquote on the next line.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>On an empty blockquote line</td>
        <td>Pressing Enter ends the blockquote.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Native Shortcuts</h2>

  <p>
    Because Ash renders a standard <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code>, all native browser
    and OS text-editing shortcuts work as expected:
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Shortcut</th>
        <th>Action</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + Z</code></td>
        <td>Undo</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + Z</code> (or <code>Ctrl + Y</code>)</td>
        <td>Redo</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + A</code></td>
        <td>Select all</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd/Ctrl + C / X / V</code></td>
        <td>Copy / Cut / Paste</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Home / End</code></td>
        <td>Jump to start / end of line</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Cmd + Home / End</code></td>
        <td>Jump to start / end of document</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>Option/Alt + ←/→</code></td>
        <td>Move by word</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Adding Custom Shortcuts</h2>

  <p>
    Use the <code>onKeyDown</code> prop to add your own shortcuts. Ash always
    calls your handler after processing its own shortcuts — even when Ash
    handled the key. Check <code>e.defaultPrevented</code> if you need to know
    whether Ash already acted on the event:
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`<Editor
  value={text}
  onChange={setText}
  onKeyDown={(e) => {
    // Cmd+S to save (Ash does not handle this key, so defaultPrevented is false)
    if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === 's') {
      e.preventDefault();
      save(text);
    }

    // Skip if Ash already handled the event
    if (e.defaultPrevented) return;
  }}
/>`}</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
